      "writtenOn": "2018-10-16T14:30:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a change in behaviour. Previously, CMD_REEVALUATE would wait for an existing probe to complete. But now we stop the current detection thread and start it again. Any reason you changed this?\n\nI think it would be possible to keep the existing behaviour by only keeping the thread alive in WaitForProbeCompletionState. You\u0027d start the thread in enter(), and stop in exit(). (Using enter and exit helps ensure that all codepaths in and out of the state will start or stop the thread). In WaitForProbeCompletionState you could defer all messages. I think this would be have pretty much the same as it does today.\n\nThen, in the future, you could make WaitForProbeCompletionState process some messages while it\u0027s running. That way, when NetworkMonitor needs to do things that are unrelated to probing, it can still do them.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 724,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 727,
        "endChar": 21
      },
