      "writtenOn": "2018-10-16T14:30:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: sleeping slows down the tests and can cause it to be flaky if the device is busy and doesn\u0027t finish the operation in time.\n\nDid you consider using a CountDownLatch or ConditionVariable to avoid sleeping? That would require ensuring that when sendProbeResult is called, we count down the latch. Not sure how to do that with a spy. But perhaps you do this by making the test a bit more realistic. You could create a very simple handler that only knows how to process the CMD_PROBE_COMPLETE method. When it sees that message, it would count down the latch. Then you could pass that handler into makeMonitor().\n\nI think you need to create a looper for that to work, but there are examples of that in several tests.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
